From: Tao Gong <gongtao0607@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 05:46:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mt7530: trap frames to conduit in MFC on
 EN7581 and AN7583

On MT7531 and MT7988, trapped frames are forwarded to the CPU ports in
the MT7531_CFC CPU_PMAP bitmap. EN7581 and AN7583 support was added on
the assumption that they follow the MT7531 model, so only CFC is set and
mt753x_conduit_state_change() returns early for them.

On EN7581 this is not enough: frames trapped by the BPC/RGAC registers,
such as STP BPDUs, do not reach the CPU port unless MT7530_CPU_EN and
MT7530_CPU_PORT are also set in MT753X_MFC. Ports that use the switch
(not the GDM ports of the SoC) therefore never receive BPDUs, and an STP
bridge on them takes the root role while a superior root is reachable.

Tested on an Airoha AN7581 board (Gemtek W1700K) with a user port of the
switch receiving RSTP BPDUs from the root at 1/s. With CPU_EN clear in
MFC, as the driver leaves it, no BPDU reached the CPU. Setting CPU_EN and
CPU_PORT at runtime made them arrive at once, and clearing them stopped
them again. With this patch they are received from boot.

AN7583 has the same switch IP and the same CFC handling, so it is
included as well. It was not tested.

Include EN7581 and AN7583 in mt753x_conduit_state_change() and update
the related comments.

Fixes: 2b0229f67932 ("net: dsa: mt7530: Add EN7581 support")
Fixes: d76556db10bf ("net: dsa: mt7530: Add AN7583 support")
Acked-by: Lorenzo Bianconi <lorenzo.bianconi@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Tao Gong <gongtao0607@gmail.com>
---
Index: linux-6.18.55/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
===================================================================
--- linux-6.18.55.orig/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
+++ linux-6.18.55/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
@@ -1283,8 +1283,8 @@ mt753x_cpu_port_enable(struct dsa_switch
 		   UNU_FFP(BIT(port)));
 
 	/* Add the CPU port to the CPU port bitmap for MT7531 and the switch on
-	 * the MT7988 SoC. Trapped frames will be forwarded to the CPU port that
-	 * is affine to the inbound user port.
+	 * the MT7988, EN7581 and AN7583 SoCs. Trapped frames will be forwarded
+	 * to the CPU port that is affine to the inbound user port.
 	 */
 	if (priv->id == ID_MT7531 || priv->id == ID_MT7988 ||
 	    priv->id == ID_EN7581 || priv->id == ID_AN7583)
@@ -3195,10 +3195,12 @@ mt753x_conduit_state_change(struct dsa_s
 
 	/* Set the CPU port to trap frames to for MT7530. Trapped frames will be
 	 * forwarded to the numerically smallest CPU port whose conduit
-	 * interface is up.
+	 * interface is up. EN7581 and AN7583 need this in addition to the CPU
+	 * port bitmap, or trapped frames never reach the CPU port.
 	 */
 	if (priv->id != ID_MT7530 && priv->id != ID_MT7621 &&
-	    priv->id != ID_EN7528)
+	    priv->id != ID_EN7528 &&
+	    priv->id != ID_EN7581 && priv->id != ID_AN7583)
 		return;
 
 	mask = BIT(cpu_dp->index);
